  "attribution": "Written by a model from the explanatory memorandum; not the record",
  "describes_version": "original",
  "as_of": "2015-06-03",
  "sentences": [
   "The bill would authorise cost recovery levies for imported food administration where the charges are classified constitutionally as customs duties.",
   "Regulations would prescribe the matters attracting charges, set amounts or calculation methods and identify who must pay, alongside existing fees for individual services.",
   "It would accompany separate general and excise charging bills and a collection bill, with substantive operation linked to commencement of the collection arrangements."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "Charges would require ministerial satisfaction that they recover no more than likely Commonwealth costs.",
   "Regulations could exclude specified matters from charging.",
   "The framework would prohibit taxation of state-owned property.",
   "Christmas Island and the Cocos Islands would be covered only if the imported food control legislation extends there."
  ],
  "affected": "Food importers and businesses handling imported food would be affected.",
